\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The 92.4\,GHz frequency union comprises 34{} disjoint islands of median width 1.8\,GHz, concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, and the summed window bandwidth exceeds the union by a factor 7.6 -- coverage narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited, not broad. The occurrence limits of \S  \ref  {sec:discussion} are conditioned on these intervals. Thresholds are nominal in the sense of \S  \ref  {sec:method}.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{2}{5}{What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The \UnionGHz \,GHz frequency union comprises \UnionIntervals {} disjoint islands of median width 1.8\,GHz, concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, and the summed window bandwidth exceeds the union by a factor 7.6 -- coverage narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited, not broad. The occurrence limits of \S \ref {sec:discussion} are conditioned on these intervals. Thresholds are nominal in the sense of \S \ref {sec:method}}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Design of the survey. All public execution blocks on the 168{} targets are mined from the ALMA archive, positions propagated to each epoch from Gaia\nobreakspace  {}DR3, and searched along the two independent lanes described in the text. Solid borders mark validated components; the validation rail summarises the injection-recovery (1200{} trials, Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:inject}), chirp/periodicity and frequency-occupancy analyses.}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{3}{6}{Design of the survey. All public execution blocks on the \NCensus {} targets are mined from the ALMA archive, positions propagated to each epoch from Gaia~DR3, and searched along the two independent lanes described in the text. Solid borders mark validated components; the validation rail summarises the injection-recovery (\NTrials {} trials, Appendix~\ref {app:inject}), chirp/periodicity and frequency-occupancy analyses}{figure.3}{}}
