\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Selection function of the searched sample against a volume-limited reference census. Census: Gaia\nobreakspace  {}DR3 sources with $\varpi >0$, $\sigma _\varpi /\varpi \le 0.1$ and $1/\varpi \le 40$\,pc (17566 objects; 8594, 49 per cent, carry a \texttt  {teff\_gspphot} estimate). Sample: the 85{} stars with at least one searched window in this release. Sample distances are those used by the search itself and are complete; temperatures exist for 51 of the 85{} stars (all 85 matched to the 168-entry ALMA-covered census, 56 by exact name; 51 of those matches carry a temperature), so the temperature panel is normalised within each column over classified objects only and $T_{\rm  eff}$ proxies spectral class. ``Ratio'' is the sample column fraction over the census column fraction: 1 means the sample tracks the reference population, $>1$ over-representation.}}{25}{table.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:selfunc}{{15}{25}{Selection function of the searched sample against a volume-limited reference census. Census: Gaia~DR3 sources with $\varpi >0$, $\sigma _\varpi /\varpi \le 0.1$ and $1/\varpi \le 40$\,pc (17566 objects; 8594, 49 per cent, carry a \texttt {teff\_gspphot} estimate). Sample: the \NStars {} stars with at least one searched window in this release. Sample distances are those used by the search itself and are complete; temperatures exist for 51 of the \NStars {} stars (all 85 matched to the 168-entry ALMA-covered census, 56 by exact name; 51 of those matches carry a temperature), so the temperature panel is normalised within each column over classified objects only and $T_{\rm eff}$ proxies spectral class. ``Ratio'' is the sample column fraction over the census column fraction: 1 means the sample tracks the reference population, $>1$ over-representation}{table.15}{}}
